ers, observers, kept data) are checked on line only (lifecycle.browser.test.ts); for this type they are checked only through the controller in Node.\",\n    \"compact\": \"In a browser, the one-turn sequence, the rejected strict update and what destroy() releases (the element, listeners, observers, kept data) are checked on line only (lifecycle.browser.test.ts); for this type they are checked only through the controller in Node.\"\n  }\n}\n{\n  \"id\": \"P7\",\n  \"pending\": {\n    \"line\": \"Not measured for this revision: the benchmark harness in bench/ exists; the acceptance measurements wait for a quiet machine (STATUS.md, 2026-11-18). Its endpoints P7-mem and P7-lifecycle (bench/src/decision.js) are not measured; the tests cited as weak each bound one part of the budget on line only. The harness's P7-lifecycle endpoint runs 2,500 cycles and gates on at most 1% heap growth, and the Chrome heap test compares two window means with a 1% allowance: neither shows the spec's \\\"no upward slope\\\" over 1,000 cycles, since a small positive slope passes both.\",\n    \"area\": \"Not measured for this revision: the benchmark harness in bench/ exists; the acceptance measurements wait for a quiet machine (STATUS.md, 2026-11-18). The harness's memory workloads draw a line; no test bounds this chart type's owned bytes or its heap over create–destroy cycles. The harness's P7-lifecycle endpoint runs 2,500 cycles and gates on at most 1% heap growth, and the Chrome heap test compares two window means with a 1% allowance: neither shows the spec's \\\"no upward slope\\\" over 1,000 cycles, since a small positive slope passes both.\",\n    \"bar\": \"Not measured for this revision: the benchmark harness in bench/ exists; the acceptance measurements wait for a quiet machine (STATUS.md, 2026-11-18). The harness's memory workloads draw a line; no test bounds this chart type's owned bytes or its heap over create–destroy cycles. The harness's P7-lifecycle endpoint runs 2,500 cycles and gates on at most 1% heap growth, and the Chrome heap test compares two window means with a 1% allowance: neither shows the spec's \\\"no upward slope\\\" over 1,000 cycles, since a small positive slope passes both.\",\n    \"scatter\": \"Not measured for this revision: the benchmark harness in bench/ exists; the acceptance measurements wait for a quiet machine (STATUS.md, 2026-11-18). The harness's memory workloads draw a line; no test bounds this chart type's owned bytes or its heap over create–destroy cycles. The harness's P7-lifecycle endpoint runs 2,500 cycles and gates on at most 1% heap growth, and the Chrome heap test compares two window means with a 1% allowance: neither shows the spec's \\\"no upward slope\\\" over 1,000 cycles, since a small positive slope passes both.\",\n    \"donut\": \"Not measured for this revision: the benchmark harness in bench/ exists; the acceptance measurements wait for a quiet machine (STATUS.md, 2026-11-18). The harness's memory workloads draw a line; no test bounds this chart type's owned bytes or its heap over create–destroy cycles. The harness's P7-lifecycle endpoint runs 2,500 cycles and gates on at most 1% heap growth, and the Chrome heap test compares two window means with a 1% allowance: neither shows the spec's \\\"no upward slope\\\" over 1,000 cycles, since a small positive slope passes both.\",\n    \"compact\": \"Not measured for this revision: the benchmark harness in bench/ exists; the acceptance measurements wait for a quiet machine (STATUS.md, 2026-11-18). The harness's memory workloads draw a line; no test bounds this chart type's owned bytes or its heap over create–destroy cycles. The harness's P7-lifecycle endpoint runs 2,500 cycles and gates on at most 1% heap growth, and the Chrome heap test compares two window means with a 1% allowance: neither shows the spec's \\\"no upward slope\\\" over 1,000 cycles, since a small positive slope passes both.\"\n  },\n  \"weakLine\": [\n    {\n      \"kind\": \"unit\"